   "reason": "UNL-N01..N06 (dev3-tree-smo.md#unlink-u4): the U3 review history (CREATE, A's autocommit INSERT of 11 or 8 of the largest rows at q 2, autocommit DELETEs of the leftmost leaf's three rows at q 3..5 retired by C's Row-only cleanup, then A's cleanup drain asking C's live unlink). The memory twins run it over the memory directory for LeafUnlink and RootCollapse and restart (recover with an empty Commit at q 6, then reenter) from the files when the drain starts (N01's state, no unlink byte) and after the durable unlink (N04's state), walking the recovered tree from T's anchor (literal keys, level, XTR1 list, routed or listed T pages with no orphan, allocator entries, structural claims, bank high-water) and reading the kept rows through B. unl_n_inventory_states_the_module_rule checks the frozen inventory (include_str) against the worker's rule. The ignored unlink_native_worker is the same history, one same-ELF process per phase; scripts/check_dev3_unlink_native.py ran 38 processes PASS (module-gate/evidence/dev3-08-1-unlink-u4/run). unlink_rows.rs only declares the module.",
